Z||000000||btoth||03-29-2001||04:24 PM||||Well, Midas just called... they can't install the Flowmaster because it won't fit.  (#42583) But before he gave up he said that he called some Fiero people in Texas that said not to do it.  They told him that they've successfully installed the Flowmaster but that the customers come back complaining about rattles from the muffler hitting parts of the car.<P>Well, I do have the better dogbone mount so my engine barely moves at all, but does anyone else have their Flowmaster rattle???  For as much as this guy says he like Fieros, I'm beginning to think he's full of sh*t.<P>For those of you that have the Flowmasters (or other performance mufflers), how'd you get your's installed?  And are there any problems with it?<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-29-2001||04:33 PM||||drive it down here... I'll get ya set up!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and you can even crash at my place over the weekend||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||03-29-2001||05:21 PM||||Chris Wests Flowmaster is what I have, the prices are rediculous but it sounds great!!! Pretty deep through acceleration!! I went to monroe muffler and they ran a 2-1/4" system for about 80.00 parts and labor I think it was a good deal since I do not have a welder and I didnt have to hastle with it!!<P><BR>Good Luck,<BR>Dan<P><BR>P.S. Also check out the Spintech that C West is supposively (sp?) selling at a cheaper rate||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||03-29-2001||05:23 PM||||I have a Spintech. Single 2.5" in and dual 2" out although a 2.5" out is available. It fits in the stock space fine. They couldn't install the springs on the muffler so they added two more hangers. Works fine. Doesn't hit anywhere (including the 2.5" pipes).<P>Spintech 331SC (2" out) or 333SC (2.5" out). Far more tolerable in noise than the Flowmaster too.<P>I paid $140 including tax (CA) and shipping and had it in three days. They are on the web. Call first and tell them what you are doing because they shorten the standard 331/333 down to 13". These are high quality mufflers.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||03-29-2001||05:25 PM||||Yeah, mine rattles sometimes when I start up. Doesn't bug me. That's what loud stereos are for.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||btoth||03-29-2001||05:39 PM||||Well, just picked up the car.  My car was the only one at the place today and they all looked bored.  It seems that they probably wouldn't have even installed it if I said I didn't care about the rattle.  He said that he couldn't use the the factory springs, etc.  I'm not surprise, but why couldn't they just do a custom hanger job?  Hm.  Oh well, no point getting all pissed off over a muffler I guess.||||reg||1
