Z||000012||DXR_DAD||03-29-2001||11:38 PM||||? just a quick question here, What type shops do most take there cars to?? We have the type cars that most of the "known franchise type shops" don't want to work on anyway!!! Here on this side of the map we have more "hot rod/speed shops", custom shops<BR>these are the people that can get the job done. And as we all know many many fiero owners have the flowie's on there cars, so yes it will fit! When you walk into a shop and the guy has a shoe horn in his hand trying to get a 302 into a Triumph TR6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>that guy won't say....It won't fit!!!<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000013||DougV||03-30-2001||12:56 AM||||I had a 80 series flowmaster installed with a new high-flow cat and 2 1/2 custom pipes from downpipe back done at a local custom exhaust shop for under $500 and it sounds awesome. Any no-name custom shop will have no problem doing it, the flowmaster fits fine, and does'nt come close to hitting anything. ||||reg||1
